1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Most study apps stop at the right answer — this one starts from what you can teach.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A middle-school science app where students teach an AI companion.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Your turn to teach — the textbook is hidden while you explain.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
{\an8}On-device check: did the key ideas make it into your explanation?

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
{\an8}Miss them and he asks for more — no points lost, just another try.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,000
{\an8}The key terms he caught, chip by chip.

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
{\an8}Then he asks a cataloged follow-up — never a free-form chat.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,500
Pick the answer that matches what he believes…

9
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:54,000
A miss costs a heart, records the gap, and triggers a hint — never the answer.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:60,000
Re-explain with the hint — same method, second try.

11
00:00:60,000 --> 00:00:70,000
Then compare your version against the textbook yourself.

12
00:00:70,000 --> 00:00:78,700
Only progress is recorded — the explanation itself is never stored.

13
00:00:78,700 --> 00:00:88,800
{\an8}The karte: 29 canonical misconceptions — the miss you just saw is already recorded.

14
00:00:88,800 --> 00:00:97,800
{\an8}Plus perk: a parent-ready report of what your teaching fixed.

15
00:00:97,800 --> 00:00:109,800
{\an8}Optional Plus via RevenueCat — store unreachable, so purchases stay safely blocked.
